==English==

===Etymology===
Suggested to be a clipping of ''commodity bag'', a British naval term.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[bag]] used to carry one's personal effects or [[toiletries]] while traveling.
# A [[sailor]]'s small bag to hold [[thread]], [[needle]]s, [[tape]], etc.; a [[housewife]].
#:{{syn|en|sailor's housewife}}
# A [[Girl Guides| Girl Guide's]] bag to hold dishes and cutlery. It is usually made of [[net|mesh]] fabric or sewn [[dishtowel]]. Also called a mess bag, [[dilly bag]], or [[mess kit]], depending on region.
# {{lb|en|theatre}} A bag used to hold costume pieces that do not hang on hangers, such as socks or gloves.

